<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: #ffffff; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Our Traditional Style of Dress – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Traditional Style of Dress</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Theme:</b> She Is Wearing a Pollera.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: productive: Provide instructions for developing a hands-on project. interactive: Collaborate with peers to plan a simple presentation.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can provide oral instructions to a peer for creating traditional clothing (e.g., 'First, cut the paper. Next, fold it. Then, draw the pollera.'). Can collaborate with peers to create a presentation about the cultural importance of traditional clothing with simple reasons (e.g., 'People wear polleras at festivals.'). Can describe cultural clothing with peers to enhance group understanding (e.g., 'People wear traditional clothing to celebrations.').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a variety of large, colorful flashcards or realia of different Panamanian traditional clothing (pollera, montuno, cutarras). Teacher points to a picture of a woman in a pollera and asks, "What is she wearing?" The teacher encourages students to shout out responses or raise hands. (Expected: 'Pollera!', 'Dress!').</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher explicitly models the target structure "She is wearing a pollera." and "He is wearing a montuno." The teacher repeats the sentences, emphasizing the /w/ sound in 'wearing' and the blending of /dr/ /ɛs/ for 'dress'. The teacher points to different parts of the clothing (e.g., 'jewelry', 'flowers') and says, "She is wearing beautiful jewelry." Teacher gestures to show the meaning of 'wearing'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher shows a picture of someone wearing pants and a t-shirt: "Is she wearing a pollera?" (Expected: "No!")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher shows a picture of a pollera: "Is this a modern dress or traditional clothing?" (Expected: "Traditional!")</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Our Traditional Style of Dress".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short animated video or a sequence of illustrated steps (picture cards) showing how to make a simple paper doll wearing a pollera. The visual input will be accompanied by simple, clear oral instructions narrated by the teacher or a recording. The material focuses on giving and following instructions, using vocabulary like 'cut', 'fold', 'draw', 'use', 'sew' (conceptually, not literally sewing in class, but as part of the description of traditional clothing creation).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Interacting orally to comprehend and produce simple instructions and descriptions related to cultural attire.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What are we making in this video/with these pictures?" (Expected: "A paper pollera!" or "A doll with traditional clothing!").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Teacher states, "First, we draw the flowers." (while pointing to the 'cut' step). Students respond "False!" or "True!".</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching:</b> The teacher holds up a picture of a finished paper pollera and asks, "What is this for?" Students respond based on previous lessons, e.g., "For a celebration!" "For an event!"</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Speaking to describe traditional clothing using Present Continuous ('She is wearing...'), Present Simple ('People wear...', 'It represents...'), WH-questions ('What are you wearing?'), and vocabulary (attire, celebration, event, community, traditional clothing, jewelry, festive, beautiful, cultural, important, admire, explain, showcase).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Sentence Completion (Oral):</b> The teacher displays sentences with blanks on the board or flashcards. Students complete the sentences orally, focusing on the present continuous. E.g., "She ______ a beautiful pollera." (wearing). "They ______ traditional clothing for the event." (are wearing). Teacher monitors pronunciation, especially /w/ in 'wearing'.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice - Picture Description (Pair Work):</b> Students work in pairs. Each pair receives a set of picture cards showing different people wearing traditional Panamanian clothing or engaged in a cultural celebration. One student picks a card and describes it using "She is wearing..." or "He is wearing..." and target vocabulary like 'festive', 'jewelry', 'cultural attire'. The partner listens and points to the correct picture or asks a simple WH-question like "What is she wearing?". The teacher circulates, providing support and correcting pronunciation, including blending /pr/ /ɪt-i/ for 'pretty'.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Guided Pair Interaction - Explaining Significance:</b> Still in pairs, students look at the picture cards again. This time, they take turns briefly explaining why people wear this clothing. E.g., "People wear polleras at festivals. It is important for our community." or "This attire represents our culture." Teacher encourages the use of 'present simple' and prepositions 'at' and 'in'.</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Our Traditional Style of Dress".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Mini-Presentation / Giving Instructions. Students work in small groups (3-4). Each group chooses one of two options:
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Option 1: "How to Make a Paper Pollera"</b> – Groups prepare to orally demonstrate and provide simple step-by-step instructions to their peers on how to 'make' a simple paper pollera (using pre-cut shapes or drawing). E.g., "First, cut the paper. Next, fold it. Then, draw the pollera." They use verbs like 'cut', 'fold', 'draw', 'use'.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Option 2: "Our Traditional Clothing"</b> – Groups prepare a simple oral presentation describing one traditional Panamanian attire (e.g., the pollera). They must explain what it is, what people wear it for (celebrations, events), and why it is important for their community. E.g., "This is a pollera. Women wear it at festivals. It is beautiful and cultural." They use vocabulary like 'showcase', 'represent', 'admire', 'community'.</li>
                </ul>
                Students must collaborate to plan their oral delivery, ensuring everyone speaks. The teacher walks around, listening, facilitating, and encouraging natural communication.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during group presentations/instructions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students present their chosen option (instructions or description) to the class or to another group. Each student in the group must contribute orally.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist):</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation (e.g., /w/ in 'wearing', clear words).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (e.g., 'pollera', 'celebration', 'beautiful', 'fold').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of Present Continuous ('She is wearing...') and Present Simple ('People wear...').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of instructions/description (easy to understand).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaboration with peers (all group members participate).</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a quick oral or written exit ticket:
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new word I used today was ______."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can now say 'She is wearing a ______' (name one traditional clothing item)."</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">7-8 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of our presentation/instructions was the easiest to say in English?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one thing I want to improve about my speaking in English?"</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in terms of student engagement and speaking practice? (e.g., collaborative tasks, visual aids).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for next lesson to support students' writing skills, especially concerning sentence construction and description of traditional clothing? (e.g., more sentence frames, review of simple present tense).</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> This speaking lesson provided practice in describing traditional clothing and explaining its cultural significance. For Lesson 4 (Writing), students will use the vocabulary and grammatical structures (Present Continuous, Present Simple) to write short descriptions or instructions about traditional clothing, building on their oral practice today.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>